 mod(m, n, d)","page":6},{"level":3,"title":"4.20.5 tan(x)","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"5 Calculating the Television Lighting Consistency Index (TLCI)","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 Principle of the TLCI (Informative)","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 TLCI Calculation process","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 Determining the spd of the Reference Luminaire","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.1 Calculation of Correlated Color Temperature (CCT) of the Test Luminaire","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.2 Determining the spd of the Reference Luminaire","page":11},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.1 Selection of Reference Luminaire","page":11},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.2 Planckian radiator","page":11},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.3 Daylight radiator","page":12},{"level":4,"title":"5.3.2.4 Mixed radiator","page":12},{"level":2,"title":"5.4 Color Samples","page":13},{"level":2,"title":"5.5 Reference Camera","page":14},{"level":2,"title":"5.5.1 Definition of Reference Camera","page":14},{"level":2,"title":"5.5.2 Applying the responsivity of the reference camera","page":14},{"level":2,"title":"5.5.3 White balance","page":15},{"level":2,"title":"5.5.4 Reference Camera Matrix","page":16},{"level":2,"title":"5.5.5 Reference Camera saturation control","page":16},{"level":2,"title":"5.5.6 Opto-electronic transfer characteristic","page":16},{"level":2,"title":"5.6 Reference Display","page":17},{"level":2,"title":"5.6.1 Overview","page":17},{"level":2,"title":"5.6.2 Electro-optical transfer characteristic","page":17},{"level":2,"title":"5.6.3 Display Synthesis Matrix","page":17},{"level":2,"title":"5.7 Color-difference Calculations","page":18},{"level":2,"title":"5.7.1 Calculation of CIEDE2000 color differences","page":18},{"level":2,"title":"5.7.2 Calculation of the RP 2093 TLCI value, Qa","page":18},{"level":2,"title":"5.7.3 Interpretation of Qa (Informative)","page":19}],"definitions":[{"term":"CIE 1931 standard observer","definition":"ideal observer whose color-matching properties co